    "finding": {
        "narrative": "The biometric de-duplication consumer failed while building the candidate refId-to-UID map for an update request: BioDataBaseHelperServiceImpl.getUidOriginTrackerData found no UidOriginTracker row for one of the matched candidates and raised BusinessException [UID_ORIGIN_TRACKER_DATA_NOT_FOUND]. The service documentation lists this code as a business exception on the PostEnrolment (Bio Fraud) path: the lookup treats an absent origin-tracker row as fatal, so every retry fails the same way until the row exists. The logs corroborate the trace: the same exception and code appear on the failing consumer's ERROR line inside the retry window, with no other error for the packet.",
